{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3516","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3516","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3516\",\"parent_revision\":\"1d0c4f9d31bf37047d5395dbd1610327c4b4b8c3a0363b2e4fc9bdfa26710dbf\",\"root_revision\":\"1d0c4f9d31bf37047d5395dbd1610327c4b4b8c3a0363b2e4fc9bdfa26710dbf\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-13\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nresearch-curator's PR #3513 wires check-backlinks --fix into the shared Post-Actions step as a trusted per-run gate for all four modes. Two gaps surfaced by Codex review during that PR make its exit code and coverage less trustworthy than the new caller assumes:\\n\\n1. build_cross_reference_graph() in backlink_lib.py catches OSError (unreadable file) and ValueError (malformed Cross-References table) per-file with no warning emitted -- its own docstring states paths that cannot be resolved are \\\"silently skipped.\\\" check-backlinks calls this same function for both its initial scan and its post-repair verification scan, and reports exit 0 whenever no asymmetric edges remain in the graph it built. If the scan silently dropped some files due to a read or parse error, exit 0 means \\\"no known-bad edges in what was successfully scanned,\\\" not \\\"the whole vault was verified\\\" -- a false completeness signal.\\n\\n2. check-backlinks --fix has no per-file exclude/skip mechanism -- it operates on the whole vault directory with no way to keep it from touching a specific target file. A caller that wants to avoid writing into a file with pre-existing uncommitted changes from another contributor can only detect and exclude that file from its own commit after check-backlinks has already run and potentially written to it, not prevent the write in the first place.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible fixes suggested during the PR #3513 review discussion -- (1) make build_cross_reference_graph/check_backlinks surface or fail on scan-phase read/parse errors instead of swallowing them silently, so a clean exit code is a trustworthy completeness signal; (2) add an --exclude/--skip-path option (or equivalent) to check-backlinks so a caller can keep it from writing to specific files at all.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Claim:** `build_cross_reference_graph()` catches `OSError` and `ValueError` per file with no\\n  warning emitted.\\n  **verdict:** REFUTED\\n  **Evidence:** `backlink_lib.py:628-651` prints `warning: scan-skipped, could not read|parse|resolve ...`\\n  to stderr for all three failure classes, gated by the `quiet` flag. Commit `bf54394` (#3529)\\n  introduced these warnings after this item was filed on 2026-09-13.\\n\\n- **Claim:** Exit 0 from `check-backlinks` means \\\"no known-bad edges in what was successfully\\n  scanned\\\", not \\\"the whole vault was verified\\\".\\n  **verdict:** VERIFIED\\n  **Evidence:** `validate_research.py:1117-1156` \u2014 `check_backlinks()` derives its exit code only\\n  from `find_asymmetric_edges()`. No skip count reaches the caller, because\\n  `build_cross_reference_graph()` returns `dict[Path, list[Path]]` and nothing else.\\n\\n- **Claim:** The `build_cross_reference_graph()` docstring states that unresolvable paths are\\n  \\\"silently skipped\\\".\\n  **verdict:** VERIFIED\\n  **Evidence:** `backlink_lib.py:611` Returns block. The statement is now stale \u2014 warnings are\\n  printed unless `quiet=True`.\\n\\n- **Claim:** `check-backlinks --fix` has no per-file exclude mechanism.\\n  **verdict:** VERIFIED\\n  **Evidence:** `validate_research.py:1109-1112` \u2014 the command signature accepts `vault_path` and\\n  `--fix` only.\\n\\n- **Claim:** `check-backlinks --fix` runs as a trusted per-run gate for callers.\\n  **verdict:** VERIFIED\\n  **Evidence:** `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md:339` invokes it in Post-Actions.\\n  `references/entry-review-rubric.md:27,34` treats its exit code as the reciprocity gate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Date:** 2026-09-13\\n\\n**Decision:** APPROVED\\n\\n| Condition | Status |\\n|---|---|\\n| Current behaviour of `build_cross_reference_graph()` | AVAILABLE \u2014 read at `backlink_lib.py:592-655` |\\n| Current behaviour of `check_backlinks()` exit paths | AVAILABLE \u2014 read at `validate_research.py:1108-1158` |\\n| Full caller set | AVAILABLE \u2014 repository-wide grep, five call sites |\\n| Existing test coverage for scan-skips | AVAILABLE \u2014 `test_locator_and_scan_resilience.py:175-209` |\\n| Which of the two reported gaps still hold | AVAILABLE \u2014 resolved by the Fact-Check section above |\\n\\n**Note:** Gap 1 as filed is partly stale. Warnings now exist. The untrustworthy exit code and the\\nstale docstring remain.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type:** defect\\n\\n**Rationale:** The item names two observable behaviours of shipped code \u2014 an exit code that does\\nnot reflect scan-phase skips, and a missing CLI option. Both are checkable against source.\\n\\n**Analysis method:** Direct source read of `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/backlink_lib.py`\\nand `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py`, plus `git log -S`.\\n\\n**Scenario target:** `check-backlinks` exits 0 after silently dropping files from the scan.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Systems Inventory**\\n\\n| System | Path | Change |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Graph builder | `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/backlink_lib.py` | Return scan-skip records alongside the graph; correct the stale docstring |\\n| CLI command | `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` | Report skips, fail on them, add an exclusion option |\\n| Tests | `tests/research_backlinks/test_locator_and_scan_resilience.py` | Existing scan-skip tests call `build_cross_reference_graph()` directly \u2014 a changed return type touches them |\\n| Tests | `tests/research_backlinks/test_validator_cli.py`, `test_idempotency.py` | Assert `check-backlinks` exit codes |\\n| Skill docs | `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md`, `references/cross-reference-format.md`, `references/entry-review-rubric.md` | Document the new option and the stricter exit code |\\n\\n**Direct callers of `build_cross_reference_graph()`:** `validate_research.py` (two call sites in\\n`check_backlinks`) and the three test modules above. No other caller exists in the repository.\\n\\n**Risk:** Medium. A stricter exit code turns pre-existing unreadable or malformed entries into\\ngate failures for every caller of `check-backlinks`, including `research-curator` Post-Actions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Priority:** P2\\n\\n**Effort:** S \u2014 two scripts, one test module, three documentation files. No new dependency.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Alignment assessment:** ALIGNED\\n\\n`AGENTS.md` requires avoiding silent failure paths (`rules/silent-failure-prevention.md`) and\\ntreating a clean gate as evidence of an actual check. Making the exit code reflect scan coverage\\nserves both. The exclusion option serves `AGENTS.md` \\\"Working Tree Safety\\\", which requires not\\nwriting over another contributor's uncommitted work.\\n\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `build_cross_reference_graph()` reports which files it skipped, so a caller can act on it.\\n2. `check-backlinks` prints the scan-skip count on stdout in the same machine-readable\\n   `key: value` form as `asymmetric_cross_references`.\\n3. `check-backlinks` exits non-zero when any file was skipped during the scan, so exit 0 means the\\n   whole vault was verified.\\n4. A flag suppresses criterion 3 for callers that accept a partial scan, and its name and\\n   behaviour are documented.\\n5. `check-backlinks` accepts a repeatable exclusion option that prevents `--fix` from writing to a\\n   named path.\\n6. An excluded path is still scanned and still counted in the reported asymmetric pairs \u2014 the\\n   option gates writes only.\\n7. Existing tests in `tests/research_backlinks/` pass, and new tests cover criteria 2 through 6.\\n8. `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` and `references/entry-review-rubric.md` state the new\\n   exit-code rule and the exclusion option.\\n9. The `build_cross_reference_graph()` docstring no longer claims skips are silent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Create a vault with two entries that cite each other, plus one `.md` file with a malformed\\n   Cross-References table.\\n2. Run `uv run --script .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py check-backlinks <vault>`.\\n3. Observe `warning: scan-skipped` on stderr, `asymmetric_cross_references: 0` on stdout, and exit\\n   code 0.\\n\\nCovered at the library level by `test_locator_and_scan_resilience.py::test_scan_skip_warning_prints_a_vault_relative_path`,\\nwhich asserts the warning but not the exit code.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`build_cross_reference_graph()` returns only the adjacency dict. A file dropped during the scan\\nleaves no value in the return type, so `check_backlinks()` has nothing to inspect. Its exit code\\nis computed from `find_asymmetric_edges(graph)` alone. A scan-skip therefore shrinks the graph and\\nmakes a clean result more likely, not less.\\n\\n`check_backlinks()` accepts `vault_path` and `fix` only. No parameter carries an exclusion set, so\\n`_repair_one_asymmetric_pair()` writes to every asymmetric target in the vault.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"50071fccc56634e2dd4f9cc42497b87cb6c0b175ae251cb97b12d167660b9d46\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUeTQOQ\"}"}